      "final_text": "Done. `lake build Solution` exits 0 with no errors and no `sorry`.\n\nWhat changed (only [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean)):\n\n- **Fix**: `VyperSqrt.sqrt` is now `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)` \u2014 the PR 4486 min-choice \u2014 instead of the v0.4.0 `p.2` port that rounded up on raw `9999999998`.\n- **New lemmas**: `trap_entry_min` (first trap index via minimal-counterexample induction), `sqrt_eq_of_bounds` (floor uniqueness from two-sided bounds, handling `N \u2264 1` and `N \u2265 2` separately), `loop_final` (deployed loop lands in `{s, s+1}\u00b2` minus `(s+1, s+1)`; the `a = seed` case resolves to `a \u2208 {9999999999, 10000000000}` with both root bounds by `decide`), `sqrt_correct_nat`, and `sqrt_zero`.\n- **Proofs**: all 5 required theorems with exact names/statements, covering negative inputs (revert), `x = 0`, and positive decimals bridged from `Nat.sqrt (a\u00b710^10)` bounds to `r\u00b7r \u2264 x\u00b7DIVISOR < (r+1)\u00b7(r+1)` via casts.\n\nVerification observed: clean build; `grep` finds none of the forbidden tokens; `#print axioms` shows `sqrt`, `req_sqrt_neg_reverts`, `req_deployed_loop` depend on nothing and the other three on exactly `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; `git status` shows only `candidate/Solution.lean` modified; both probe files removed. The 3 remaining warnings are pre-existing unused-variable notes in untouched code.",
